/code-review high — loop R1, round 2 — range 7bb533f8..d0aa95ae (branch 2026-10-08-mockups-served-at-a-url)

[
  {"file": "plugins/vwf/skills/mockups/scripts/lib/routes.mjs", "line": 323,
   "summary": "GET / returns an empty 404 whenever no screen of the platform has the route `/`. Yet /vwf:mockups step 9 tells the user to open that bare root URL, which it calls \"the app's / screen\".",
   "failure_scenario": "Take a mobile platform whose screens are /home and /signin, or whose screens are all unrouted /<code>-<slug>. matchPath(root, routes, '/') gets no hit from findScreen. walk then yields only the root, which has no index.html, so the result is {kind:'none'} and the server sends a blank 404. The one URL the reviewer is given is dead, and the page has no overlay and no link to /__mockups/."},
  {"file": "plugins/vwf/skills/blueprint/references/screen-review.md", "line": 39,
   "summary": "Pages left at a route that has since moved are never pruned. §6a has no prune step and a flow-scoped /vwf:mockups run deletes only paths that routes.json still names. links.mjs still scans those old pages, and none of them has an owning flow to re-dispatch.",
   "failure_scenario": "A pass changes 200a's route from /orders/list to /orders. The old orders/list/index.html stays on disk. links.mjs walks every .html, so it flags that page's links to routes that moved. Step 1.3 is to 'send each to the generator of the flow that owns the page (its screen in routes.json)', but no screen owns orders/list. After 2 rounds the review stops with no URL and no flows_rendered stamp. Meanwhile the server keeps serving the old page at its old URL."},
  {"file": "plugins/vwf/skills/mockups/scripts/links.mjs", "line": 81,
   "summary": "The link check reads only `href`, but the generator is told it may navigate with a form `action`. A form action is therefore never checked, and a POST form is refused by the server.",
   "failure_scenario": "The generator writes <form action=\"/ordres/1042\" method=\"post\">, either a typo or a contract-faithful POST. links.mjs reports LINKS OK. The reviewer clicks submit, which the overlay deliberately lets through. A typo gets a 404. A POST gets 415, because refusal() demands application/json, or 404, because only /comment and /done accept POST. Either way the 'every link works' guarantee is broken."},
  {"file": "plugins/vwf/skills/mockups/scripts/routes.mjs", "line": 129,
   "summary": "routeToken takes the first whitespace token that starts with `/` anywhere in the Route cell, so prose that names another route becomes this screen's route.",
   "failure_scenario": "A modal row has the Route cell 'modal over `/orders`'. The backticks are stripped, the token becomes /orders, and it collides with the real /orders screen. routes.mjs reports 'route /orders is held by two codes' and exits 1. Every flow of that platform renders nothing, even though the contract is valid. Without the collision, the modal would have silently overwritten the list page's folder."},
  {"file": "plugins/vwf/skills/mockups/scripts/routes.mjs", "line": 117,
   "summary": "A home-rule reference row is skipped only when the Code cell itself is a markdown link. The doctrine says only that a touching flow 'links the home flow's row' and does not say which cell carries the link.",
   "failure_scenario": "Flow 300 references screen 100a as | 100a | [Home](../100-home/web.md#screens) | / | ... |. The code is plain, so the row is not skipped. routes.mjs reports 'code 100a is defined twice' and 'route / is held by two codes', exits 1, and the whole platform gets no mockups and no review."},
  {"file": "plugins/vwf/skills/mockups/SKILL.md", "line": 208,
   "summary": "/vwf:mockups reports every `status: open` item in comments.yaml. The file survives every render, /vwf:mockups never closes a comment, and §6a deliberately leaves instruction-like comments open. §6a also turns comments on other flows' screens into proposals, because it serves the whole platform.",
   "failure_scenario": "Comments from round 1 on screens that have since been re-rendered or re-routed are listed again on every later /vwf:mockups run, so the report grows without bound. In a §6a pass for flow 200, a comment left on 100a while browsing the connected site becomes a 'proposed Screens-contract change' to flow 100, which is outside the pass's scope."},
  {"file": "plugins/vwf/skills/mockups/scripts/serve.mjs", "line": 410,
   "summary": "`new URL(req.url, base)` is called with no try/catch inside the synchronous request handler, so a malformed request target throws and kills the review server.",
   "failure_scenario": "Any local client sends `GET //[ HTTP/1.1` with Host 127.0.0.1:<port>. new URL throws ERR_INVALID_URL, the exception is uncaught, the process exits non-zero mid-review and the session loses the Done signal. Also, `GET //x/orders` is read as host 'x' plus path /orders, so it serves a different path than the one requested. An appendFileSync error inside the async postComment would likewise end as an unhandled rejection that crashes the server."},
  {"file": "plugins/vwf/skills/mockups/scripts/serve.mjs", "line": 562,
   "summary": "The overlay returns early for any a[href] and any submit control, so the reviewer can never select a link or a primary button to comment on it, including the `href=\"#\"` placeholders the generator emits.",
   "failure_scenario": "The reviewer wants to say 'this CTA label is wrong' about <a href=\"/orders/1042\">View order</a> or <a href=\"#\">Cancel</a>. The click navigates, or does nothing, and the comment form never opens. The most review-relevant elements, the navigation and actions, cannot be commented on."},
  {"file": "plugins/vwf/skills/mockups/scripts/routes.mjs", "line": 159,
   "summary": "The collision key is case-sensitive, but the tree is written to a case-insensitive filesystem (APFS). Two routes that differ only in case map to the same folder and are not reported.",
   "failure_scenario": "Screen 200a has /Orders and screen 300a has /orders. byPath sees two distinct keys, so routes.json is written with no error. On macOS both generators write to one orders/index.html and the second overwrites the first. One screen's mockup silently replaces the other's, and both URLs serve the same page."},
  {"file": "plugins/vwf/skills/mockups/scripts/serve.mjs", "line": 431,
   "summary": "matchPath already computes the screen, but it does not return it, so serve.mjs calls findScreen over the whole route list again for every served page.",
   "failure_scenario": "This is duplicated matching logic: every HTML GET scans routes.screens twice. The overlay's code also comes from a second lookup that can diverge from the one that chose the file. Returning `screen` from matchPath's file and placeholder results would remove the second call and keep one source of truth."}
]
